1. Difference between Frontend, Backend, and Full-Stack Development
Frontend Development:-
Frontend is the part of a website that users can see and interact with. It includes the design, buttons, menus, images, and layout. It is mainly built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
Backend Development:-
Backend is the part that works behind the scenes. It manages data, user accounts, databases, and server-side logic. Technologies like Node.js, Java, Python, and MySQL are commonly used.
Full-Stack Development:-
A full-stack developer works on both the frontend and backend. They can build and manage the complete web application.
Example:-
In an online shopping website, the product page is the frontend, the login and payment system are handled by the backend, and a full-stack developer can build both parts.

3. How a Browser Requests and Displays a Web Page
When a user enters a website URL, the browser sends an HTTP request to the web server. The server processes the request and, if needed, gets data from the database. It then sends the webpage files back to the browser. Finally, the browser displays the webpage for the user.

